' Source evidence (Java before alignment a7f78fed): only the last-message retention fix existed.
' Reviewed Java baseline bf28e72f: compaction retry did not persist its discarded Entry identity.
' Implemented Java baseline bd26e7f8: Agent.buildStreamOptions, RuntimeEntryCodec.effectiveContextEntries,
' RuntimeEventProjector.projectCompactionCompleted, and SessionCompactor.decide.
' Observed implementation: common compaction aligns request limits and restored retry context.
' Design reason: Runtime, Cron, and Child require one failure-safe context policy.
' Java divergence: append-only Entries use an internal discarded Entry ID; only Read paths are tracked.

actor Host
participant "ManagedAgentSession" as Session
participant "Agent loop" as Agent
participant "SessionCompactor" as Compactor
participant "FileOperationTracker" as Tracker
participant "Model Manager" as Model
database "Append-only history" as History

== Recover persisted overflow before accepting input ==
Host -> Session : prompt(message)
Session -> Compactor : decide restored context before prompt
opt stale ERROR or LENGTH overflow is recoverable
  Session -> Compactor : prepare without failed Assistant
  Compactor --> Session : prepared window or none
  opt prepared window exists
    Session -> Model : summarize before accepting prompt
    Model --> Session : summary and Usage
    Session -> Session : publish compacted context
  end
end
== Execute and choose compaction policy ==
Session -> Agent : execute with model max output\nwhen no caller override exists
Agent --> Session : Assistant with stop reason and Usage
Session -> Compactor : decide by same model, boundary,\noverflow, Usage, and fallback estimate
alt ERROR or LENGTH overflow and no prior recovery
  Session -> Session : remove failed Assistant from retry context
  Session -> Compactor : prepare compactable context
  Compactor -> Tracker : collect Read paths only
  alt no safe compactable window
    Compactor --> Session : none; emit no lifecycle event
  else window prepared
    Session --> Host : compaction.started\nreason=overflow, willRetry=true
    Compactor -> Model : summarize history and optional turn prefix
    alt summary succeeds
      Model --> Compactor : full summary and combined Usage
      Compactor --> Session : summary, retained messages, boundary
      Session -> History : append compaction completed\nwith internal discarded Entry ID
      Session -> Agent : retry original model call once
      Agent --> Session : final Assistant
      Session -> History : append final Assistant
      opt Host reloads the Session
        Host -> History : load current branch
        History --> Session : summary, retained, discarded, retry
        Session -> Session : exclude exact discarded Entry ID
      end
      opt second response still overflows
        Session --> Host : compaction.failed\nwillRetry=false
      end
    else summary fails or is cancelled
      Model --> Compactor : error or abort
      Compactor --> Session : failed
      Session -> Session : retain old context
      Session --> Host : compaction.failed with aborted flag
    end
  end
else STOP succeeds but Usage is already over context window
  Session -> Compactor : prepare full context including Assistant
  alt window prepared
    Session --> Host : compaction.started\nreason=overflow, willRetry=false
    Compactor -> Model : summarize successful context
    Model --> Compactor : full summary and Usage
    Compactor --> Session : summary, retained messages, boundary
    Session -> History : append compaction completed
  end
  Session --> Host : return original successful answer; no replay
else valid Usage or fallback estimate exceeds threshold
  Session -> Compactor : prepare(reason=threshold)
  opt window prepared
    Session --> Host : compaction.started\nwillRetry=false
    Compactor -> Model : summarize structured context
    Model --> Compactor : full summary and Usage
    Compactor --> Session : summary and retained messages
    Session -> History : append compaction completed
  end
end
Session --> Host : execution result

note over Session,Compactor
  Use safe User / Assistant boundaries.
  Retain the last Assistant and sorted Read paths.
  Use the actual model output limit for LENGTH
  recovery.
end note

note over Compactor,Model
  No tools or cache in summary requests.
  Invalid summaries never replace the old context.
  History remains append-only; discard IDs stay
  internal.
end note
@enduml

@startuml refresh_next_execution
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 165
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #526777
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #BAC4CC
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #8496A4
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #BAC4CC
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBEF
skinparam noteBorderColor #D2C6A5
hide footbox
autonumber
title Refresh Affects the Next Idle Session Execution

' Source evidence (CampusClaw PR 167 f60cc3e): AgentRuntimeManager refresh and Runtime Session store.
' Pending implementation Java design: RuntimeSessionModelReconciler runs before accepting user.message.
' Architecture change: refresh does not mutate an active execution snapshot.
' Design reason: make directory publication atomic while preserving execution consistency.

actor Admin
actor Caller
participant "Runtime Session\nModel Reconciler" as Reconciler
participant "Agent Runtime\nManager" as Runtime
database "Published Agent directory" as Directory
participant "Model Manager" as Models
database "Session and Entry store" as Store
participant "Execution Host" as Host

== Publish directory ==
Admin -> Runtime : refresh(agentId)
Runtime -> Directory : atomically publish validated tree
Runtime --> Admin : success
note over Host
  Any active execution keeps its existing
  snapshot.
end note

== Resolve the next idle execution ==
Caller -> Reconciler : POST next user event
Reconciler -> Directory : load latest bindingModels and default
Reconciler -> Models : resolve current model with credentials
alt current model remains callable
  Models --> Reconciler : current model
else current model is invalid
  Reconciler -> Models : resolve new default with credentials
  alt default is callable
    Models --> Reconciler : fallback model
    Reconciler -> Store : atomically update model and optional thinking
    Reconciler -> Store : append model and thinking changed entries
    Store --> Caller : project configuration events first
  else no callable default
    Models --> Reconciler : unavailable
    Reconciler --> Caller : reject before user.message
  end
end
== Accept only with a callable model ==
Reconciler -> Store : accept user.message; mark running
Reconciler -> Host : start with reconciled immutable snapshot
@enduml
